   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The two rays bound the angles of the region, so the angles run from \\( \\pi \\) to \\( \\frac{3 \\pi}{2} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99001",
         "rule_named": "limits of the sweep"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The area is one half the integral of the square of r: \\( A = \\frac{1}{2}\\int_{\\pi}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}} \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 \\theta \\right)} + 3\\right)^2\\,d\\theta \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99048",
         "rule_named": "polar area"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Expand the square and use \\( \\sin^2 u = \\tfrac{1}{2}(1 - \\cos 2u) \\) or \\( \\cos^2 u = \\tfrac{1}{2}(1 + \\cos 2u) \\) to integrate, giving \\( A = \\frac{19 \\pi}{8} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Rational",
               19,
               8
            ],
            "Pi"
         ],
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99004",
